Subject: [PATCH] Review-first defaults for Development Intelligence

Development Intelligence's audience reviews and validates agent-written code; they don't live in
the file tree. Ship defaults that match:

- Workspace trust dialog OFF by default (sessions are server-provisioned
  workspaces the control plane already vetted; the dialog is the single worst
  first-run experience on any device — see the field history in grotto).
- Startup editor: none (the agent panel is the home surface, not a Welcome
  tour aimed at hand-coders).

Out of scope for this patch, handled elsewhere: the Development Intelligence
activity-bar container comes from the baked-in di-ide extension, and telemetry
is off because the product.json overlay ships no telemetry endpoints (OSS
builds without them report nothing).

This patch intentionally touches ONLY registered configuration defaults, not
workbench code paths, so it survives upstream rebases with trivial conflicts.
Hunks are anchored against the pinned tag in upstream.json (1.96.4); index
lines are the real 1.96.4 blob hashes so `git apply --3way` can fall back to
a content merge on small upstream drift. Re-anchor with `build.sh --check`
after every tag bump.

---
 .../welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.contribution.ts | 2 +-
 .../contrib/workspace/browser/workspace.contribution.ts          | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.contribution.ts b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.contribution.ts
index e5b5899..366f81d 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.contribution.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.contribution.ts
@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ configurationRegistry.registerConfiguration({
 				localize({ comment: ['This is the description for a setting. Values surrounded by single quotes are not to be translated.'], key: 'workbench.startupEditor.welcomePageInEmptyWorkbench' }, "Open the Welcome page when opening an empty workbench."),
 				localize({ comment: ['This is the description for a setting. Values surrounded by single quotes are not to be translated.'], key: 'workbench.startupEditor.terminal' }, "Open a new terminal in the editor area."),
 			],
-			'default': 'welcomePage',
+			'default': 'none', // Development Intelligence: the agent panel is the home surface, not a Welcome tour
 			'description': localize('workbench.startupEditor', "Controls which editor is shown at startup, if none are restored from the previous session.")
 		},
 		'workbench.welcomePage.preferReducedMotion': {
diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/workspace/browser/workspace.contribution.ts b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/workspace/browser/workspace.contribution.ts
index 0ab6828..85adcd1 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/workspace/browser/workspace.contribution.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/workspace/browser/workspace.contribution.ts
@@ -730,7 +730,7 @@ Registry.as<IConfigurationRegistry>(ConfigurationExtensions.Configuration)
 		properties: {
 			[WORKSPACE_TRUST_ENABLED]: {
 				type: 'boolean',
-				default: true,
+				default: false, // Development Intelligence: no trust dialogs -- workspaces are provisioned by the control plane
 				description: localize('workspace.trust.description', "Controls whether or not Workspace Trust is enabled within VS Code."),
 				tags: [WORKSPACE_TRUST_SETTING_TAG],
 				scope: ConfigurationScope.APPLICATION,
